IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja2-part4-ad-civil`

-- Tests for the Appellate Division civil module (ss 35 to 45). Expected values are written from the text of the sections, not from the code.

`test: the order of a decision` MEANS Order WITH
    about IS `permission to defend proceedings`
    `way it went` IS `granted unconditionally`

GIVEN court IS A Court
      jurisdiction IS A `Jurisdiction exercised`
      nature IS A `Nature of the proceeding`
GIVETH A Decision
`test: a decision made by` MEANS Decision WITH
    `made by` IS court
    `in the exercise of` IS jurisdiction
    `nature of the proceeding` IS nature
    `subject of the case` IS `any other civil matter`
    `the order` IS `test: the order of a decision`
    `made after the trial of an action` IS TRUE
    `made by consent of the parties` IS FALSE
    `amount in dispute or value of the subject matter, excluding interest and costs` IS NOTHING
    `date made` IS Date 1 3 2025
    `date the judgment or order was extracted` IS NOTHING
    `a written law provides that it is final or that no appeal lies` IS FALSE
    `the parties agreed in writing, signed by or for each, that it is final` IS FALSE

-- s 35(1)
#ASSERT (`s 35(1) this Division applies to the Appellate Division` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 35(1) this Division applies to the Appellate Division` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 35(2)(a): a civil decision of the General Division in original or appellate civil jurisdiction
#ASSERT (`s 35(2)(a) the matter is an appeal against a decision of the General Division in a civil cause or matter` (`test: a decision made by` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding`) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 35(2)(a) the matter is an appeal against a decision of the General Division in a civil cause or matter` (`test: a decision made by` `General Division` `appellate jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding`) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- supervisory jurisdiction is neither original nor appellate
#ASSERT (`s 35(2)(a) the matter is an appeal against a decision of the General Division in a civil cause or matter` (`test: a decision made by` `General Division` `supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding`) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a criminal proceeding is not a civil cause or matter
#ASSERT (`s 35(2)(a) the matter is an appeal against a decision of the General Division in a civil cause or matter` (`test: a decision made by` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a criminal proceeding`) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- K4: a quasi-criminal proceeding is not a civil cause or matter (the Act sorts proceedings into three kinds, s 20); the list is closed by "consists of"
#ASSERT (`s 35(2)(a) the matter is an appeal against a decision of the General Division in a civil cause or matter` (`test: a decision made by` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a quasi-criminal proceeding`) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not an appeal at all
#ASSERT (`s 35(2)(a) the matter is an appeal against a decision of the General Division in a civil cause or matter` (`test: a decision made by` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding`) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a decision of the District Court: the text names the General Division
#ASSERT (`s 35(2)(a) the matter is an appeal against a decision of the General Division in a civil cause or matter` (`test: a decision made by` `District Court` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding`) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- K1: a decision of the Singapore International Commercial Court is not settled
#ASSERT (`s 35(2)(a) the matter is an appeal against a decision of the General Division in a civil cause or matter` (`test: a decision made by` `Singapore International Commercial Court` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding`) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 35(2)(b)
#ASSERT (`s 35(2)(b) the matter is an appeal or other process that lies, or is transferred, to the Appellate Division` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 35(2)(b) the matter is an appeal or other process that lies, or is transferred, to the Appellate Division` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 35(2)(b) the matter is an appeal or other process that lies, or is transferred, to the Appellate Division` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 35(2): the two limbs together
#ASSERT (`s 35(2) the matter is one of the matters of the civil jurisdiction of the Appellate Division` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 35(2) the matter is one of the matters of the civil jurisdiction of the Appellate Division` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 35(2) the matter is one of the matters of the civil jurisdiction of the Appellate Division` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 35(2) the matter is one of the matters of the civil jurisdiction of the Appellate Division` NOTHING (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 35(2) the matter is one of the matters of the civil jurisdiction of the Appellate Division` NOTHING (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 36(1): "if the Seventh Schedule so provides" (the answer of the Schedule is an input)
#ASSERT (`s 36(1) the case may be heard and decided by that number of Judges` 1 (JUST TRUE) (JUST `a single Judge or 2 Judges`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 36(1) the case may be heard and decided by that number of Judges` 2 (JUST TRUE) (JUST `a single Judge or 2 Judges`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 36(1) the case may be heard and decided by that number of Judges` 3 (JUST TRUE) (JUST `a single Judge or 2 Judges`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 36(1) the case may be heard and decided by that number of Judges` 2 (JUST TRUE) (JUST `2 Judges`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 36(1) the case may be heard and decided by that number of Judges` 1 (JUST TRUE) (JUST `2 Judges`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 36(1) the case may be heard and decided by that number of Judges` 1 (JUST TRUE) (JUST `a single Judge`)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 36(1) the case may be heard and decided by that number of Judges` 2 (JUST TRUE) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the Seventh Schedule does not allow fewer than 3 Judges in this kind of case: the "if" is not met
#ASSERT (`s 36(1) the case may be heard and decided by that number of Judges` 1 (JUST FALSE) (JUST `a single Judge or 2 Judges`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 36(1) the case may be heard and decided by that number of Judges` 2 (JUST FALSE) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- whether the Seventh Schedule allows fewer than 3 Judges is not answered: the answer is NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 36(1) the case may be heard and decided by that number of Judges` 2 NOTHING (JUST `2 Judges`)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 36(1) the case may be heard and decided by that number of Judges` 3 NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 36(2)
#ASSERT (`s 36(2) the Judge may sit in the Appellate Division to hear or decide the application` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 36(2) the Judge may sit in the Appellate Division to hear or decide the application` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 36(3)(a) and (b): constituted by 3 or more, one or more unable; every party consents and at least 2 remain
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(a) the Appellate Division must continue to hear and decide the case` 5 1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(b) the case must be reheard` 5 1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- boundary: exactly 2 Judges remain
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(a) the Appellate Division must continue to hear and decide the case` 3 1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(b) the case must be reheard` 3 1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- only 1 Judge remains
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(a) the Appellate Division must continue to hear and decide the case` 3 2 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(b) the case must be reheard` 3 2 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a party does not consent
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(a) the Appellate Division must continue to hear and decide the case` 3 1 FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(b) the case must be reheard` 3 1 FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no Judge unable: the "where" is not met
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(a) the Appellate Division must continue to hear and decide the case` 3 0 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(b) the case must be reheard` 3 0 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- constituted by 2 Judges: the "where" is not met
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(a) the Appellate Division must continue to hear and decide the case` 2 1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 36(3)(b) the case must be reheard` 2 1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 37(1)
#ASSERT (`s 37(1) the Appellate Division may decide the matter without hearing oral arguments` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 37(1) the Appellate Division may decide the matter without hearing oral arguments` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 37(2): oral evidence is given, unless all the parties consent. No oral evidence given: the prohibition is not triggered and the grant-named function is silent (NOTHING); the bar twin below says JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 37(2) the part of the proceeding where oral evidence is given may be conducted without an oral hearing` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 37(2) the part of the proceeding where oral evidence is given may be conducted without an oral hearing` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 37(2) the part of the proceeding where oral evidence is given may be conducted without an oral hearing` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 37(2) the part of the proceeding where oral evidence is given may be conducted without an oral hearing` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the bar-phrased twin: oral evidence is given and the parties do not all consent: the bar applies
#ASSERT (`s 37(2) the bar on conducting the part of the proceeding without an oral hearing applies` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the unless is met: the bar is lifted
#ASSERT (`s 37(2) the bar on conducting the part of the proceeding without an oral hearing applies` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no oral evidence is given: the bar does not apply
#ASSERT (`s 37(2) the bar on conducting the part of the proceeding without an oral hearing applies` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 37(2) the bar on conducting the part of the proceeding without an oral hearing applies` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 37(3), (4), (5)
#ASSERT (`s 37(3) the Appellate Division may direct that the matter be heard in an asynchronous manner by exchange of written correspondence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 37(3) the Appellate Division may direct that the matter be heard in an asynchronous manner by exchange of written correspondence` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 37(4) the bar on hearing the matter in an asynchronous manner applies to the Appellate Division` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 37(4) the bar on hearing the matter in an asynchronous manner applies to the Appellate Division` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 37(5) the Appellate Division may hear oral arguments before deciding the matter` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 37(5) the Appellate Division may hear oral arguments before deciding the matter` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 38(1): on its own motion; any one of the three limbs
#ASSERT (`s 38(1) the Appellate Division may summarily dismiss the appeal or application on its own motion` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 38(1) the Appellate Division may summarily dismiss the appeal or application on its own motion` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 38(1) the Appellate Division may summarily dismiss the appeal or application on its own motion` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 38(1) the Appellate Division may summarily dismiss the appeal or application on its own motion` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 38(1) the Appellate Division may summarily dismiss the appeal or application on its own motion` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 38(2)
#ASSERT (`s 38(2) the Appellate Division has met the requirements before summarily dismissing, as the section requires` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 38(2) the Appellate Division has met the requirements before summarily dismissing, as the section requires` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 38(2) the Appellate Division has met the requirements before summarily dismissing, as the section requires` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 38(3), (4)
#ASSERT (`s 38(3) the Appellate Division may exercise its powers under this section without hearing oral arguments` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 38(3) the Appellate Division may exercise its powers under this section without hearing oral arguments` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 38(4) the thing is an appeal or an application for the purposes of this section` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 38(4) the thing is an appeal or an application for the purposes of this section` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 38(4) the thing is an appeal or an application for the purposes of this section` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 38(4) the thing is an appeal or an application for the purposes of this section` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 39: an application that may be made either to the General Division or to the Appellate Division must first be made to the General Division
#ASSERT (`s 39 the application must first be made to the General Division` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 39 the application must first be made to the General Division` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 39 the court to which the application must first be made` TRUE) EQUALS JUST `General Division`
#ASSERT (`s 39 the court to which the application must first be made` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 40(1): the pending matter and the three kinds of direction or order
#ASSERT (`s 40(1) the Appellate Division may make the direction or order in the pending matter` TRUE `s 40(1)(a) a direction or order incidental to the pending matter not involving the decision of the pending matter`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 40(1) the Appellate Division may make the direction or order in the pending matter` TRUE `s 40(1)(b) an interim order to prevent prejudice to the claims of the parties pending the determination of the pending matter`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 40(1) the Appellate Division may make the direction or order in the pending matter` TRUE `s 40(1)(c) an order for security for costs, or for the dismissal of the pending matter for default in furnishing security so ordered`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 40(1) the Appellate Division may make the direction or order in the pending matter` TRUE `s 40(1) another direction or order`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 40(1) the Appellate Division may make the direction or order in the pending matter` FALSE `s 40(1)(a) a direction or order incidental to the pending matter not involving the decision of the pending matter`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 40(2), (3), (4)
#ASSERT (`s 40(2) the Appellate Division may make the direction or order on its own motion or on the application of a party` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 40(2) the Appellate Division may make the direction or order on its own motion or on the application of a party` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 40(2) the Appellate Division may make the direction or order on its own motion or on the application of a party` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 40(3) the direction or order may be made by that number of Judges` 2) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 40(3) the direction or order may be made by that number of Judges` 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 40(4) the direction or order may be made by a single Judge` 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 40(4) the direction or order may be made by a single Judge` 2) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 40(4)(a) the direction or order may be varied or discharged by those Judges` TRUE 2) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 40(4)(a) the direction or order may be varied or discharged by those Judges` TRUE 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 40(4)(a) the direction or order may be varied or discharged by those Judges` FALSE 2) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 40(4)(b): permission is needed to apply to vary or discharge, and the decision is final
#ASSERT (`s 40(4)(b) an application to vary or discharge the direction or order may be made` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 40(4)(b) an application to vary or discharge the direction or order may be made` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 40(4)(b) an application to vary or discharge the direction or order may be made` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 40(4)(b) the decision to give or refuse permission is final` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 40(4)(b) the decision to give or refuse permission is final` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 40(5) section 32(1) does not stand in the way of the direction or order` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 40(5) section 32(1) does not stand in the way of the direction or order` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 41(1) to (7)
#ASSERT (`s 41(1) the appeal is by way of rehearing` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(1) the appeal is by way of rehearing` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 41(2) the Appellate Division has the power or duty of the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(2) the Appellate Division has the power or duty of the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 41(2) the Appellate Division has the power or duty of the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 41(3) the Appellate Division may receive further evidence in that manner` `s 41(3)(a) by oral examination in court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(3) the Appellate Division may receive further evidence in that manner` `s 41(3)(b) by affidavit`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(3) the Appellate Division may receive further evidence in that manner` `s 41(3)(c) by deposition taken before an examiner or a commissioner`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(3) the Appellate Division may receive further evidence in that manner` `s 41(3)(d) in any other manner that the Appellate Division allows`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(3) the Appellate Division may receive further evidence in that manner` `s 41(3) in a manner that the Appellate Division does not allow`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 41(4): only with the permission of the court and on special grounds, except as provided in subsection (5)
#ASSERT (`s 41(4) the further evidence may be given to the Appellate Division` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(4) the further evidence may be given to the Appellate Division` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 41(4) the further evidence may be given to the Appellate Division` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 41(4) the further evidence may be given to the Appellate Division` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 41(4) the further evidence may be given to the Appellate Division` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the bar-phrased twin: subsection (5) does not apply and the permission and special grounds are not both present: the bar applies
#ASSERT (`s 41(4) the bar on giving the further evidence to the Appellate Division applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(4) the bar on giving the further evidence to the Appellate Division applies` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(4) the bar on giving the further evidence to the Appellate Division applies` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- permission and special grounds both present: the bar is lifted
#ASSERT (`s 41(4) the bar on giving the further evidence to the Appellate Division applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- subsection (5) applies: the bar does not
#ASSERT (`s 41(4) the bar on giving the further evidence to the Appellate Division applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 41(5) the further evidence may be given to the Appellate Division without permission` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(5) the further evidence may be given to the Appellate Division without permission` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 41(6) the Appellate Division may draw any inference of fact, give any judgment and make any order` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(6) the Appellate Division may draw any inference of fact, give any judgment and make any order` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 41(7)(a) the power may be exercised in relation to that part of the decision appealed against` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(7)(a) the power may be exercised in relation to that part of the decision appealed against` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 41(7)(b) the power may be exercised in favour of that party` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(7)(b) the power may be exercised in favour of that party` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 41(8): a single Judge or 2 Judges decided the application
#ASSERT (`s 41(8) a party may request the full panel to rehear arguments on the application for permission to adduce further evidence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(8) a party may request the full panel to rehear arguments on the application for permission to adduce further evidence` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 41(9): no request where 2 Judges decided and 2 Judges hear the appeal, or where 3 or more Judges decided
#ASSERT (`s 41(9) the bar on a request under subsection (8) applies` 2 2) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(9) the bar on a request under subsection (8) applies` 3 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(9) the bar on a request under subsection (8) applies` 5 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(9) the bar on a request under subsection (8) applies` 2 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 41(9) the bar on a request under subsection (8) applies` 1 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 41(9) the bar on a request under subsection (8) applies` 1 2) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 41(10)(a)
#ASSERT (`s 41(10)(a) the request is made before the time at which the judgment or order is extracted` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(10)(a) the request is made before the time at which the judgment or order is extracted` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 41(10)(b): decision made on Saturday 1 March 2025, so the 7 days after the date end on Saturday 8 March 2025
#ASSERT (`s 41(10)(b) the last day of the 7 days after the date on which the decision is made` (Date 1 3 2025) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST (Date 8 3 2025)
-- 8 March 2025 a public holiday: the next day, Sunday 9 March, is excluded too, so Monday 10 March 2025
#ASSERT (`s 41(10)(b) the last day of the 7 days after the date on which the decision is made` (Date 1 3 2025) (LIST Date 8 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2025)
-- decision made on Sunday 2 March 2025: the seventh day is Sunday 9 March, which is excluded, so Monday 10 March 2025
#ASSERT (`s 41(10)(b) the last day of the 7 days after the date on which the decision is made` (Date 2 3 2025) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2025)
-- s 41(10): in time on the last day, late on the day after
#ASSERT (`s 41(10) the request under subsection (8) is made in time` (Date 8 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(10) the request under subsection (8) is made in time` (Date 9 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 41(10) the request under subsection (8) is made in time` (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- already extracted: late whatever the date
#ASSERT (`s 41(10) the request under subsection (8) is made in time` (Date 3 3 2025) TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a public holiday on the seventh day moves the last day
#ASSERT (`s 41(10) the request under subsection (8) is made in time` (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (LIST Date 8 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(10) the request under subsection (8) is made in time` (Date 11 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (LIST Date 8 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 41(11)
#ASSERT (`s 41(11) the Appellate Division may affirm, vary or set aside the decision on the application for permission to adduce further evidence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 41(11) the Appellate Division may affirm, vary or set aside the decision on the application for permission to adduce further evidence` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 42
#ASSERT (`s 42 the Appellate Division may make the order as to costs` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 42 the Appellate Division may make the order as to costs` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 43(1): a matter tried by the General Division in the exercise of its original or appellate civil jurisdiction
#ASSERT (`s 43(1) the Appellate Division may order a new trial of the matter` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 43(1) the Appellate Division may order a new trial of the matter` `General Division` `appellate jurisdiction` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 43(1) the Appellate Division may order a new trial of the matter` `General Division` `supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 43(1) the Appellate Division may order a new trial of the matter` `District Court` `original jurisdiction` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 43(1) the Appellate Division may order a new trial of the matter` `Singapore International Commercial Court` `original jurisdiction` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a matter tried in the exercise of criminal jurisdiction is outside the power's scope, and the text has no "only": NOTHING (ruling (c))
#ASSERT (`s 43(1) the Appellate Division may order a new trial of the matter` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 43(1) the Appellate Division may order a new trial of the matter` `General Division` `appellate jurisdiction` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 43(2): no new trial on the ground of an improper admission or rejection of evidence, unless it caused a substantial wrong or a miscarriage of justice
#ASSERT (`s 43(2) a new trial may be ordered on that ground` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 43(2) a new trial may be ordered on that ground` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 43(2) a new trial may be ordered on that ground` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the bar-phrased twin
#ASSERT (`s 43(2) the bar on a new trial on that ground applies` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the unless is met: the bar is lifted
#ASSERT (`s 43(2) the bar on a new trial on that ground applies` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the ground is not an improper admission or rejection of evidence: the prohibition does not reach it, and the text has no "only" (ruling (c))
#ASSERT (`s 43(2) the bar on a new trial on that ground applies` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 43(3)(a), (b): the wrong affects only part of the case or only some of the parties
#ASSERT (`s 43(3)(a) the Appellate Division may give final judgment in respect of the unaffected part of the case or the unaffected parties` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 43(3)(a) the Appellate Division may give final judgment in respect of the unaffected part of the case or the unaffected parties` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 43(3)(b) the Appellate Division may direct a new trial in respect of the affected part of the case or the affected parties` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 43(3)(b) the Appellate Division may direct a new trial in respect of the affected part of the case or the affected parties` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 43(4) the new trial may be ordered on that question without interfering with the finding or decision on any other question` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 43(4) the new trial may be ordered on that question without interfering with the finding or decision on any other question` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 44: no reversal, substantial variation or new trial on account of an error that does not affect the merits or the jurisdiction
#ASSERT (`s 44 the Appellate Division may reverse or substantially vary the decision, or order a new trial, on account of the error` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 44 the Appellate Division may reverse or substantially vary the decision, or order a new trial, on account of the error` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 44 the Appellate Division may reverse or substantially vary the decision, or order a new trial, on account of the error` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 45(1): no stay unless the court so orders
#ASSERT (`s 45(1) the appeal operates as a stay of execution or enforcement or of proceedings under the decision appealed against` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 45(1) the appeal operates as a stay of execution or enforcement or of proceedings under the decision appealed against` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the rule-phrased twin: the unless is met, so the rule does not apply
#ASSERT (`s 45(1) the rule that the appeal does not operate as a stay applies` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 45(1) the rule that the appeal does not operate as a stay applies` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 45(2): no intermediate act or proceeding is invalidated except so far as the court directs
#ASSERT (`s 45(2) the intermediate act or proceeding is invalidated` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 45(2) the intermediate act or proceeding is invalidated` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the rule-phrased twin: the exception is met, so the rule does not apply
#ASSERT (`s 45(2) the rule that no intermediate act or proceeding is invalidated applies` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 45(2) the rule that no intermediate act or proceeding is invalidated applies` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
